diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..51ae2b9 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,48 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## SMS-verified sign-up
+
+The sign-up form collects account details and an international phone number, sends
+an SMS, then submits a six-digit code to the same-origin `api/signup` endpoint.
+That endpoint checks the code with Twilio Verify before calling the existing
+registration service. No provider secrets or verification decisions are stored in
+the browser. Passwords remain in component memory until registration completes.
+
+Set these **server runtime** environment variables (see `.env.example`):
+
+- `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`
+- `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`
+- `TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID`
+
+Configure the Verify service for six-digit codes, enable SMS Fraud Guard and
+appropriate geographic restrictions, and apply service rate limits for your
+production traffic. The form includes a 30-second resend cooldown; this UI control
+is not a substitute for provider-side abuse controls. Missing configuration fails
+closed with a service-unavailable message; there is no fake or development code.
+
+For automatic code extraction, serve over HTTPS and configure an approved
+[domain-bound SMS template](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/verification-templates)
+as the Verify service’s default SMS template. Use the actual frontend hostname
+(without a scheme or path). The SMS must end with
+an origin-bound line such as `@example.com #123456`, with the actual code. Configure
+the hostname separately for each deployment. The client starts a
+[WebOTP](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp) request before
+sending the SMS, and aborts it on submission, phone edits, unmount, or timeout.
+The input also uses `autocomplete="one-time-code"` for platform SMS suggestions.
+Typing and pasting work on browsers without WebOTP, or if the user declines it.
+
+The existing remote registration service is outside this repository. To enforce
+phone verification for **all** account creation, that service must also require a
+trusted server credential/verification proof and reject direct public unverified
+registrations. Confirm that it persists the `phoneNumber` field. This application
+only calls it after provider approval; a browser flag cannot bypass that check.
+If registration fails after a code is consumed, the user is asked to request a new
+code. No live SMS delivery is required by the automated tests.
+
+Run the isolated server and phone-validation tests with Node 22.18+:
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/signup.test.ts
+```
